# Default tag vocabulary for `archive tag`.
#
# Copied to <home>/tags.rec on first use; edit that copy freely. Each tag's
# Description is what the embedding model compares folders against, so write
# it as the kinds of things such a folder contains. Several phrasings help.
# Describe content, not the medium: words like "photos" or "files" make every
# photo folder look alike.

%rec: Tag
%key: Name
%mandatory: Name Description

Name: family
Description: family life: relatives, children, babies, parents, grandparents, family gatherings at home

Name: travel
Description: travel and holidays: trips, sightseeing, landmarks, temples, beaches, mountains, foreign cities and countries

Name: celebration
Description: celebrations and events: christmas, birthdays, weddings, anniversaries, parties, graduations

Name: pets
Description: pets and animals: cats, dogs, puppies, kittens, birds, horses

Name: nature
Description: nature and outdoors: landscapes, gardens, flowers, hiking, wildlife, sunsets

Name: food
Description: food, cooking, recipes, restaurants, meals, baking

Name: vehicles
Description: cars, motorbikes, bicycles, trains, planes and other vehicles

Name: home
Description: house and home: renovation, furniture, rooms, moving house, garden projects

Name: people
Description: friends and people: portraits, groups, gatherings, reunions

Name: work
Description: work and career: jobs, office, meetings, presentations, business documents

Name: school
Description: school and study: university, courses, homework, lecture notes, theses

Name: code
Description: software source code and programming projects, scripts, repositories

Name: electronics
Description: electronics and hardware projects: circuits, schematics, PCBs, firmware, microcontrollers

Name: design
Description: design and art files: drawings, CAD models, 3D printing, graphics, illustrations

Name: music
Description: music and audio: songs, recordings, albums, podcasts, sound files

Name: video
Description: video recordings, films, movies, home movies

Name: documents
Description: scanned documents and paperwork: letters, forms, manuals, receipts

Name: legal
Description: legal and identity documents: contracts, certificates, passports, wills, deeds

Name: finance
Description: money and finance: bank statements, taxes, invoices, insurance, payslips

Name: health
Description: health and medical records, prescriptions, test results

Name: backup
Description: backups and exports: phone backups, email archives, account exports, ISO files, zip archives

Name: games
Description: games and gaming: save files, mods, screenshots, game projects
